+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-specialtydirectory-001"></a>
+
+The clinic also publishes the inverse view of that directory (confirmed 2026-08-15): every specialty it knows, each with the veterinarians holding it. A specialty is shown by the name the clinic has stored for it. A veterinarian is named in full, first name before last name. The page lists specialties rather than the whole roster, so a veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on it. Every specialty is shown together on one page `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]`. The page is reached by its own address alone: no page links to it, and the navigation gains no entry for it.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every stored specialty is listed by its stored name.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given a specialty that veterinarians hold, when the directory is opened, then each of those veterinarians is named under it by first name and last name.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on the page.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given more specialties than one veterinarian-directory page would show, when the specialty directory is opened, then all appear on one page with no paging control.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given the specialty directory, when it is rendered, then it carries the navigation every page carries, and no entry for itself is added anywhere.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given the supported languages, when the page's wording is checked, then every piece of it is present in each of them.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty that no veterinarian holds is still listed, with no veterinarian shown under it.
+2. A veterinarian holding two specialties is shown under each of them.
+3. Specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
